    "updated_at": "2022-11-30T10:44:45Z",
    "body": "> Now furthermore, I see now that \"apply the history step\" clears it across origins always. It's not clear to me that clearing the name for auxiliary browsing contexts in that matter is web compatible. I don't think that's something any user agents do or have active plans to do.\r\n\r\nThe full conditions are\r\n\r\n> - navigable's [parent](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nav-parent) is null;\r\n> - targetEntry's [document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#she-document)'s [browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-bc) is not an [auxiliary browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#auxiliary-browsing-context) whose [disowned](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#disowned-its-opener) is false; and\r\n> - targetEntry's [document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#she-document)'s [origin](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin) is not oldOrigin\r\n\r\nSo it's more strict than that. It looks like that was working to reflect https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6628#issuecomment-857535762.",
